      'class A {\npublic:\n  A() {\n    cout << "A" << endl;\n  }\n};\n\nclass B : public A {\npublic:\n  B() {\n    cout << "B" << endl;\n  }\n};\n\nint main() {\n  B b;\n  return 0;\n}',
      'Each constructor prints its own letter. The parent runs first.',
